p (e.g. only one of three valid trials analysed, or one trial and G3 missing); 0.5 = only one partial achievement: G1 with g but no multi-point fit (two arbitrary measured points), or a traceable multi-point fit over own or openly declared genuine points with g determined from it but no measured-point graph at all, or a measured-point graph (with or without fitted line) but no g; 0 = no graph- or fit-based determination (e.g. mean of 2x/t² quotients), or misconception."
